Fix a build failure with glibc 2.28 and later: the makedev macro expands
to an expression with balanced parentheses, so the extra closing
parenthesis in partimage's own definition breaks it.

Backported from the Debian partimage package
(debian/patches/04-fix-FTBFS-glic-2.28.patch), original patch from Gentoo
by Mike Frysinger <vapier@gentoo.org>, Debian bug #915987.

diff --git a/src/client/misc.h b/src/client/misc.h
index 2ec4b63..15567f0 100644
--- a/src/client/misc.h
+++ b/src/client/misc.h
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ struct COptions;
 #endif
 
 #ifndef makedev
-  #define makedev(maj,min) (((maj) << 8) | min))
+  #define makedev(maj,min) (((maj) << 8) | (min))
 #endif
 
 // =======================================================
